description:
Found by the s525q binder dual-run, perl t/op/write.t:2224 (`foreach my $e ( [...], [...] ) { @E = @$e; ... }` at FILE level, while a HASH `%e` (`"$e{a}"`, :326) puts the bare name `e` in _rename_spanning_lexicals' %spanning text pre-filter): `_ref_shadowed` (via _canon_refs_in < _rename_spanning_lexicals) answers 0 (not shadowed) for the body's `$e`; the binder answers 1 -- the use binds the loop variable declared in the SAME top statement (perly.y:519, the loop variable lives to the end of the loop).

Cause (read, Pl/Parser2.pm _ref_shadowed_0): the walk climbs Block -> Compound -> segment parent and asks `_stmt_binding` only of SIBLING statements before each ancestor; a declaration in a compound's HEAD (`foreach my $e`, `while (my $x = ...)`, `if (my $x = ...)`) is inside the Compound, never a sibling, so it is invisible.  `_binding_at` has `_head_binding` for exactly this; `_ref_shadowed` has no twin of it.

Probe (scratch/s525q/probes/E4.pl in the s525q worktree):

    my %e = (a => 1);
    package Other;
    print "h=$e{a}\n";
    package main;
    sub peek { print defined $main::e ? "global e set\n" : "global e undef\n" }
    my @c;
    foreach my $e ([1], [2]) { my @E = @$e; peek(); push @c, sub { $e->[0] }; }
    print join(",", map { $_->() // 'u' } @c), "\n";

The D row reproduces (PCL_BINDER_CHECK=log: E4.pl:8 and :10, ref_shadowed 0 vs 1), but perl 5.40.3 and base (main 81ef05e5) print the same (h=1 / global e undef x2 / 1,2): the loop variable is renamed by another mechanism (`$e__excl__0`).  In write.t itself the emission is `(p-foreach ($e ...) :dyn)` + `(p-defcell $e)` -- the loop variable became a dynamic cell -- but PCL dies at write.t's formline (not supported) long before the loop runs, so no wrong value is observable there.

Legacy bug, BENIGN as measured (a wrong fact, no wrong value found).  Belongs to 1c (the span consumer asks the binder).  NOT fixed in s525q (inert batch).
